# PostgreSQL & Migrations

## Database

PostgreSQL 18. Use native features where documented in ERD: partial indexes, `json` columns for metadata.

## Migration rules

- One concern per migration. Anonymous migration classes (Laravel 13 default).
- FK columns indexed. Composite indexes for tenant list queries — see `docs/multi-tenant/database-erd.md` §8.
- Partial index example: `time_logs (task_id) WHERE client_invoice_item_id IS NULL`.
- Money: `decimal(12,2)` totals, `decimal(8,2)` hours. Currency default `BDT` (3-char string).
- Soft deletes: `deleted_at` on `projects`, `tasks`, `client_invoices`.

## Laravel 13 model patterns

- `casts()` method (not `$casts` property). Constructor promotion for DI.
- Enum columns cast to backed enums in `app/Features/*/Enums/`.
- Factories in `database/factories/{Feature}/{Model}Factory.php` with states (`active()`, `draft()`, etc.).

## Before writing schema

Run Boost `database-schema` for existing tables. Cross-check indexes against ERD — do not duplicate FK indexes.
